  "Description":          "Speaks a Text Object. Two SubAIMs, Text-To-Speech and Speech Object Delivery, and no code of its own. It exists so that the User Agent can talk to the user without talking to an AIM: the UA writes text to a boundary port and the Controller does the rest, which is what zero trust requires. NOTE: this is an implementation-local AIW, not an MPAI-specified AIM; the UAG prefix marks it as belonging to the User Agent rather than to MPAI-MMC.",

